From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:39:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] winemetal: placement-heap buffers, a released-object record
 for native faults, optional stale-binding check

- MTLDevice_heapBufferSizeAndAlign and MTLHeap_newBufferAtOffset (slots 139-140):
  buffers placed in a placement heap, so D3D12 placed buffers in DEFAULT heaps
  alias the heap's memory the way D3D12 defines it. Remote mode answers 0 and
  callers fall back to standalone buffers.
- NSObject_release records every release that drops the last reference
  (pointer and class, lock-free 16K ring); madeira_wmt_released_class() lets the
  native fault handler name the class of an object a crashing thread touched.
  It identified an over-released MTLBuffer behind objc_release crashes in
  command-buffer storage reset.
- Optional stale-binding check (madeira.cfg stale-probe = 1): buffers freed by
  our release are remembered until a new buffer reuses the address, and every
  binding point (blit, compute, render, index/indirect, residency, buffer
  views) reports a dead handle. It located the defect (a UAV-clear fill on a
  freed placed alias); off by default.

Rebase onto upstream DXMT: upstream already has both placement-heap buffer
calls (MTLDevice_heapBufferSizeAndAlign at slot 126, MTLHeap_newBuffer at
128, both remote-guarded to answer 0). Madeira's slots 139-140 are not
carried: MTLHeap_newBufferAtOffset is a PE-side wrapper over upstream's
MTLHeap_newBuffer, and Madeira's out-parameter MTLDevice_heapBufferSizeAndAlign
is replaced by upstream's, which returns a struct WMTSizeAndAlign. The
auto-merged wow64 and census entries for the two slots are dropped, so the
table stays at 150. The stale-binding probe's hooks from Madeira's own heap
and residency bodies moved into upstream's MTLHeap_newBuffer and
MTLResidencySet_addAllocations; the geometry-emulation draw checks sit on
upstream's named binding indices.

